  "reason": "Evidence: RNA is the dominant signal (rna_only 0.411 vs image_only 0.208), multiprofile with avgpool is the best setting so far (config_011, scgpt: 0.530), and multimodal with resnet50+weighted does not clearly beat rna_only (config_019: 0.525 ≈ config_011: 0.530). Uncertainty: We have only tested one RNA encoder (scgpt) across all experiments. It is unknown whether the learned scgpt representation is essential or whether a simpler linear projection (pca_n2000) captures the same discriminative signal. Question: config_007 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) differs from our best result config_011 only in the RNA encoder, giving a clean single-variable comparison. Why best next experiment: RNA is clearly the primary information source, so understanding whether the encoder choice matters is more fundamental than tuning image-side or fusion details. If pca_n2000 matches scgpt, it simplifies the search space and suggests the bottleneck is elsewhere (aggregation, fusion, or image contribution). If scgpt is clearly superior, it confirms we should keep scgpt and focus remaining budget on image encoder or fusion strategy. This is the highest-information single change given current evidence."
}

